From 7c96e2ee6607bc10a1b429a5da2d4216074db896 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChenghaoLiu <linkmecry@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:16:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] [LoongArch] Emit and encode PE unwind codes

Describe the prologue of non-leaf functions in the LoongArch UNWIND_INFO:
each saved register and the stack allocation becomes a 4-byte code word
recorded in prologue order, to be replayed in reverse when unwinding.

Saved registers are taken from the callee-saved info rather than parsed
out of the instruction stream, since PEI-inserted stores carry no
FrameSetup flag, and the recorded offset is the real $sp-relative
immediate.

Disable linker relaxation for COFF: R_LARCH_ALIGN fixups have no symbol
and crash the COFF writer, and relaxable branches prevent folding the
.pdata End - Begin difference. Also give the MC-side MCRegisterInfo the
SEH register numbers used by emitWinCFISaveReg.
---
